   "hypothesis_id": "p_c3d4",
   "title": "Elena works from home three days a week; the office desk is her hub",
   "prose": "Elena splits her week: Monday, Wednesday, and Friday she works from home at desk_o1 in the office. Tuesday and Thursday she commutes to the office in town (8:00\u201317:30). On WFH days her laptop, charger, pen, and notebook are at desk_o1 from about 8:30 to 17:00. On commute days they leave with her. Priya's routine is the same as any retired person: home all day, morning walk 8:00\u20139:00, afternoon errands 14:00\u201316:00. The key distinction: on Monday, Wednesday, and Friday the office (room o1) is occupied by Elena from roughly 8:30 to 17:00, and desk_o1 holds her laptop. On Tuesday and Thursday the office is empty and her gear is OUT_OF_HOUSE. What would refute it: laptop_elena sighted at coffee_table_l1 (not desk_o1) on a Monday between 10:00 and 15:00, or Elena not present in room o1 on a Wednesday afternoon.",
