   "hypothesis_id": "p_e5f6",
   "title": "Priya runs the household; Elena is a guest in her own home",
   "prose": "Priya is the active manager of the home. She cooks breakfast (6:30\u20138:00), feeds the dog, does the dishes, and handles all cleaning. Elena comes home at 17:30 and largely relaxes on the couch; she does not cook or clean. The kitchen is very active in the early morning: kettle on the counter, mugs out, cutting board in use, pan on the stove. By 9:00 the kitchen is cleared. In the evening (18:00\u201320:00) Priya cooks dinner; the kitchen is active again. Elena's items (laptop, charger, etc.) go OUT_OF_HOUSE weekdays 8:00\u201317:30. Priya never leaves the house on weekdays except a brief 8:00\u20139:00 walk. What sets this apart: the kitchen counter and sink are cluttered with cooking items (cutting_board, pan, pot, knife) between 6:30\u20138:00 and 17:30\u201319:30, and Elena is found on the couch or in the living room in the evening, not in the kitchen. What would refute it: Elena sighted in the kitchen at 19:00 on a weekday, or the cutting board at counter_k1 at 12:00 on a weekday.",
