   "markdown": "# p_789a \u2014 The dog drives the daily schedule\n\nThe dog is the centre of the household's morning and evening. Elena feeds the dog at 7:15 (before leaving for work) and Priya feeds it at 17:45 (after Elena arrives or just before). The dog bowl is on the kitchen floor at all times but is actively being filled at those moments. The dog is walked by Elena 7:00\u20137:30 (she's out the door with the dog, so she's briefly OUT_OF_HOUSE or ON_PERSON with the dog toy) and by Priya 16:00\u201316:30. During walks, the dog_toy is ON_PERSON with the walker. The dog_food_bag is at pantry_shelf most of the day but is on the kitchen floor during feeding (7:00\u20137:45 and 17:30\u201318:15). Elena's work items leave 8:00\u201317:30 weekdays. Priya is home all day. What sets this apart: the dog_food_bag is on the kitchen floor (not pantry shelf) at 7:00 and 17:30, and the dog_toy is ON_PERSON during the 16:00\u201316:30 window. What would refute it: dog_food_bag at pantry_shelf_k1 at 7:15, or dog_toy at floor_l_l1 at 16:15.\n\n```json\n{\n \"claims\": [\n  {\n   \"claim\": \"The dog food bag is on the kitchen floor during the morning feeding\",\n   \"target\": \"dog_food_bag_shared\",\n   \"expect\": \"floor_k_k1\",\n   \"days\": \"both\",\n   \"from\": 7,\n   \"to\": 7.75\n  },\n  {\n   \"claim\": \"The dog toy is being carried by Priya during her afternoon walk\",\n   \"target\": \"dog_toy_shared\",\n   \"expect\": \"ON_PERSON\",\n   \"days\": \"weekday\",\n   \"from\": 16,\n   \"to\": 16.5\n  },\n  {\n   \"claim\": \"The dog bowl is on the kitchen floor at midday\",\n   \"target\": \"dog_bowl_shared\",\n   \"expect\": \"floor_k_k1\",\n   \"days\": \"both\",\n   \"from\": 10,\n   \"to\": 14\n  },\n  {\n   \"claim\": \"Elena's laptop is out of the house at 10am on a weekday\",\n   \"target\": \"laptop_elena\",\n   \"expect\": \"OUT_OF_HOUSE\",\n   \"days\": \"weekday\",\n   \"from\": 9,\n   \"to\": 16\n  }\n ],\n \"targets\": {\n  \"dog_bowl_shared\": [\n   {\n