   "markdown": "# p_3456 \u2014 Priya leaves for errands 14:00\u201316:00; the house is often empty\n\nOn weekdays, Priya goes out for errands between 14:00 and 16:00. She takes her water_bottle_priya and sometimes her book_priya. Since Elena is at work (8:00\u201317:30), the house is completely empty between 14:00 and 16:00 on weekdays. No one is in any room. The dog is home alone (or with a neighbour\u2014this hypothesis assumes the dog stays). On weekends, Priya's walk is 10:00\u201311:00 (shorter, she takes the water bottle). Elena does her own errands 12:00\u201314:00 on weekends. What sets this apart: at 15:00 on a weekday, NO resident is in ANY room, and water_bottle_priya is NOT at dish_rack_k1. At 15:00 on a Saturday, Priya IS home. What would refute it: Priya sighted in any room at 15:00 on a Tuesday, or water_bottle_priya at dish_rack_k1 at 15:00 on a weekday.\n\n```json\n{\n \"claims\": [\n  {\n   \"claim\": \"Priya's water bottle is out of the house at 2pm on a weekday\",\n   \"target\": \"water_bottle_priya\",\n   \"expect\": \"OUT_OF_HOUSE\",\n   \"days\": \"weekday\",\n   \"from\": 14,\n   \"to\": 16\n  },\n  {\n   \"claim\": \"Priya's book is out of the house at 2pm on a weekday (she takes it for errands)\",\n   \"target\": \"book_priya\",\n   \"expect\": \"OUT_OF_HOUSE\",\n   \"days\": \"weekday\",\n   \"from\": 14,\n   \"to\": 16\n  },\n  {\n   \"claim\": \"Priya's water bottle is at the dish rack at 10am on a weekday\",\n   \"target\": \"water_bottle_priya\",\n   \"expect\": \"dish_rack_k1\",\n   \"days\": \"weekday\",\n   \"from\": 9,\n   \"to\": 12\n  },\n  {\n   \"claim\": \"Elena's laptop is out of the house at 1pm on a weekday\",\n   \"target\": \"laptop_elena\",\n   \"expect\": \"OUT_OF_HOUSE\",\n   \"days\": \"weekday\",\n   \"from\": 9,\n   \"to\": 16\n  }\n ],\n \"targets\": {\n  \"water_bottle_priya\": [\n   {\n    \"days\": \"both\",\n    \"from\": 0,\n    \"to\": 24,\n    \"at\": \"dish_rack_k1\",\n    \"chance\": \"usually\"\n   },\n